      "wpId": 50472,
      "title": "My Correlation Matrices: ETF Correlation",
      "duration": "Reading",
      "type": "text",
      "vimeoId": null,
      "contentHtml": "<p>The ETF correlation table illustrates the relationships between various exchange-traded funds (ETFs) and the SPDR S&amp;P 500 ETF (SPY). Correlation coefficients range from -0.756 to 1.000, reflecting how closely each ETF's returns align with SPY's returns.</p>\n<p>Higher positive correlations, such as DIA (0.950) and QQQ (0.950), indicate that these ETFs, which track the Dow Jones Industrial Average and the NASDAQ-100 respectively, tend to move in tandem with the broader U.S. equity market represented by SPY. Conversely, ETFs like TLT (-0.002) and UVXY (-0.756) show near-zero or negative correlations, meaning they tend to move independently or inversely relative to the S&amp;P 500. This diversity in correlation can be useful for investors seeking to build a well-balanced portfolio, allowing for risk management by including assets with different market sensitivities and behaviors.</p>\n<table style=\"width: 427px\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 147.852px;text-align: left\">Security</th>\n<th style=\"width: 269.148px;text-align: left\">SPY Correlation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">SPY</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">1.000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">DIA</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.950</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">QQQ</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.950</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">IWM</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.866</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">XLF</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.845</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">XHB</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.829</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">IYR</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.829</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">EEM</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.810</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">EWJ</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.748</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">XLU</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.693</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">EWW</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.675</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">IBB</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.592</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">XBI</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.594</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">EWZ</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.577</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">XLE</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.561</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">OIH</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.637</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">FXE</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.479</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">FXI</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.430</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">GDX</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.390</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">SLV</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.390</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">RSX</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.341</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">GLD</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.302</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">USO</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.283</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">FXY</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.139</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">UNG</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.124</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">TBT</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">0.020</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">TLT</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">-0.002</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">VXX</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">-0.725</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.852px\">UVXY</td>\n<td style=\"width: 269.148px\">-0.756</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>This list captures the securities' correlation with SPY, representing a broad range of asset classes and sectors.</p>",
